+# Security Fix: CVE-2026-25087
+
+**Package**: pyarrow 22.0.0
+**CVE**: CVE-2026-25087
+
+## Vulnerability
+
+Integer overflow and out-of-bounds read in the Apache Arrow C++ IPC reader
+(`cpp/src/arrow/ipc/reader.cc`). Buffer offsets and lengths from a crafted
+IPC record batch were not checked against the size of the IPC file area, and
+the variadic buffer count of a binary-view or string-view column was not
+checked against the buffers in the batch. The C++ sources are not in the PyPI
+sdist.
+
+## Fix
+
+`build/build.sh` and `build/build_macos.sh` clone apache-arrow-22.0.0, apply
+`build/CVE-2026-25087.patch` at -p1, and build libarrow from that tree. The
+patch:
+
+- adds overflow-checked `AddWithOverflow` / `MultiplyWithOverflow` helpers to
+  `cpp/src/arrow/util/int_util_overflow.h`;
+- rejects a buffer whose offset plus length overflows or lies past the end of
+  the IPC file area ("exceeds IPC file area");
+- reserves variadic buffers up front in `ArrayLoader::LoadCommon`, and rejects a
+  variadic buffer count larger than the buffers left in the batch (GH-48900);
+- adds `has_variadic_buffers()` to `cpp/src/arrow/type.h`.
+
+The wheel is rejected unless libarrow contains the string
+"exceeds IPC file area". This file is a marker so patch-source has a diff to
+apply to the sdist. It does not change the C++ sources.
